*** PROJECT: BUDGET APPLICATION

Summary: Build a personal budgeting application that models life in a high-cost city (NYC) on an entry-level Data Scientist salary of $85,000, netting ~70% after state and local taxes. The app will forecast evolving income and expenses—especially rent and food—by applying constant growth-rate compounding (e.g., inflation) and projecting salary progression over time. Core methods include cumulative growth modeling (compounding via cumulative products) and translating forecasted growth rates into dollar values from a chosen baseline. Deliverables: a forward-looking cash-flow plan, sensitivity to inflation/salary scenarios, and clear year-over-year projections to support strict budgeting and long-term financial planning.

A) Salary and taxes

You just got a new job as an entry-level Data Scientist at a technology company in New York City with a decent starting salary of $85,000 per year.
Unfortunately, after state and local taxes, you can expect to be sending roughly 30% back to the government each year.
You will need to calculate your monthly take home pay after taxes in order to begin budgeting.

# Enter your annual salary
